{"ts":"2026-09-04T18:24:56.659Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-1","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"d9a4ee3d3683af0351613faf","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-1","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.260","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-79gv6q"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"pm context summary counts are denominated in the returned slice, so the canonical orient cold-start reports 4 open items in a 291-item backlog"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Measured 2026-09-04 on the 2026.9.4 build against the live tracker (291 open, 65 blocked, 2631 total). pm context summary reports active_items, open, and blocked denominated in the returned slice, not the workspace: the default limit reports open 53 and blocked 14; --limit 3 reports open 4 and blocked 3; the canonical cold-start pm context --for orient reports open 4, blocked 3, and then prints total_items 2631, closed 2326, canceled 14 in the same summary block. One block therefore mixes two populations without saying so, and the intent AGENTS.md names as the measured cold-start tells a fresh agent that a 291-item backlog has four open items.\n\nThis is the read-output representativeness family applied to the summary itself: the part a bounded read returned claims a count for the part it withheld. Acceptance: summary counts are workspace-scoped (or the slice-scoped fields are renamed to say so, with the workspace count beside them); the orient and handoff intents carry both scopes explicitly; the omission receipt names summary as population-scoped; a negative control renders a slice count under a population key and fails; the truthful-context contract doc and the context intent fixtures record the field semantics."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","area:cli","area:context","context-management","output-contracts","receipts","token-budget"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-09-04T18:24:56.659Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-09-04T18:24:56.659Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Summary counts are workspace-scoped or the slice-scoped fields are renamed to say so with the workspace count beside them; The orient and handoff intents carry both scopes explicitly and the omission receipt names summary as population-scoped; A negative control that renders a slice count under a population key fails; The truthful-context contract doc and the context intent fixtures record the field semantics"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"pm-cli 2026.9.4 build against the live tracker, 2631 items"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Run pm context --json, pm context --limit 3 --json, and pm context --for orient --json on a tracker with more open items than the limit and compare summary.open with pm stats by_status.open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Summary counts describe the workspace or are named as slice counts beside the workspace figure"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"summary.open is 53, 4, and 4 for the same 291-open workspace and the orient block prints workspace totals beside slice count